{"abstract":"Perception in virtual reality is often compared to the perception of pictures. There are, however, important differences. A virtual reality environment, unlike a picture, is interactive and immersive. These properties give rise to novel theoretical challenges. Building on James J. Gibson’s analysis of the perception of depictions, we raise three questions about perception in virtual reality, to which we offer tentative answers: (1) Is virtual reality a kind of picture perception? Answer: No. A virtual reality headset is better understood not as an image-based display but as a pair of electronic spectacles that allow the wearer to sample a simulated ambient optic array. (2) Who creates the information in virtual reality? Answer: The information is a joint creation of hardware developers, software engineers, and the observer. The observer is a co-creator of the information that they detect. (3) Are there affordances in virtual reality? Answer: Yes, but there are limitations on what a given virtual reality environment can provide to its users, resulting from the details of how the environment is implemented. An accurate understanding of the perceptual information available in virtual reality may contribute to current philosophical debates on the nature of experience in virtual reality.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Baggs, Edward","Grabarczyk, Paweł","Rucińska, Zuzanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-751076"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Baggs, Edward"],"country":["Belgium","Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Antwerp","University of Łódź"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the visual information available in virtual reality","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10407413.2024.2322992","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-751076","identifier":[{"id":"85186938134","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-ea9cb914-d5fe-45e7-84de-886ab6574c56"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8ABFF0BD49EDDB302A093C8ACB783A44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/10407413.2024.2322992","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/265154196/The_Visual_Information_Available_in_Virtual_Reality.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Central Administration, Vice-Chancellor's Office, DIAS","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Centre for Human Interactivity (CHI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"pl","key":"university of łódź","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Łódź","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"be","key":"university of antwerp","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Antwerp","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Edward","key":"baggspau","last":"Baggs","locid":"d80ec636-14a3-4041-9346-7539647ab4af","name":"Baggs, Edward","orcid":"0000-0003-3203-1250","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paweł","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","name":"Grabarczyk, Paweł","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Zuzanna","key":"rucińskapau","last":"Rucińska","name":"Rucińska, Zuzanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/10407413.2024.2322992","issn":["10407413","15326969"],"issn_org":["10407413"],"issue":"1","journal":"Ecological Psychology","pages":"24-38","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"Ecological Psychology","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186938134"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-ea9cb914-d5fe-45e7-84de-886ab6574c56"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Visual Information Available in Virtual Reality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-751076","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Previous work demonstrates that students without prior program- ming experience are worse off than their programming experienced peers in terms of both Introductory Programming (CS1) grades and dropout rates. Many universities, therefore, offer an onboarding (CS0) course aimed at bridging the programming experience gap by teaching the basics of programming to inexperienced students. This paper reports on the effects of providing a three-day elective onboarding course over a period of five years (2016–2020), involving a total of N=798 software development students at the IT University of Copenhagen. The paper compares 271 students who attended versus a baseline of 527 who did not attend the onboarding course. The results show that programming inexperienced students are indeed able to “catch up” to the level of their experienced peers both in terms of CS1 grades and dropout rates. Aside from objectively increasing competence, the onboarding also increases confidence, self-efficacy and diminishes insecurities, according to onboarded participants. Finally, the results suggest that onboarding has the potential to increase the diversity of students.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383588"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Competence","Computer Science","Computing","Confidence","Diversity","Dropout","Education","Gender","Grades","Onboarding","Programming","Self efficacy","Software development"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the effect of onboarding computing students without programming confidence or experience","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/80BCA0BC6DD8438DA566DD33265AED57.ashx","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383588","identifier":[{"id":"85142937486","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9f5d636e-4b5e-4c7f-8528-219c53cee961"],"keyword":["Diversity","Gender","competence","computer science,","computing","confidence","dropout","education","grades","onboarding","programming","self-efficacy","software development"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B9546D48150984B5728729F380CE405"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://ccer.itu.dk/-/media/80BCA0BC6DD8438DA566DD33265AED57.ashx","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian Mateos","key":"nicolajsenpau","last":"Nicolajsen","locid":"e175684d-abc3-4ee4-9a12-af6c611e47c0","name":"Nicolajsen, Sebastian Mateos","orcid":"0000-0002-3498-0970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3564721.3564724","eisbn":["9781450396165"],"place":"Koli, Finland","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"ACM Proceedings of the Koli Calling International Conference on Computing Education Research","status":"p","title":"Koli Calling '22: 22nd Koli Calling International Conference on Computing Education Research"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142937486"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9f5d636e-4b5e-4c7f-8528-219c53cee961"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"On the Effect of Onboarding Computing Students without Programming-Confidence or -Experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383588","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Freiesleben, Alma","Bastrup, Amanda","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382656"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computing educational programmes with more women are more about people amp less about things","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3502718.3524784","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382656","identifier":[{"id":"85134432652","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5cb7e261-83b0-439a-8362-c0841166e74e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E93C05C5C4D3B4FE9EBA47C02C2F1644"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3502718.3524784","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Play","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design, Play, Culture and AI Section","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alma","key":"freieslebenpau","last":"Freiesleben","name":"Freiesleben, Alma","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Amanda","key":"bastruppau","last":"Bastrup","name":"Bastrup, Amanda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781450392013"],"pages":"172-178","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ITiCSE 2022: Innovation and Technology in Computer Science Education (ITiCSE 2022)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134432652"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5cb7e261-83b0-439a-8362-c0841166e74e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computing Educational Programmes with more Women are more about People &amp; less about Things","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382656","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"This article takes a deeper look at the notion of ludo-narrative dissonance (henceforth LND), a popular term that refers to the perceived clash between the ludic and the narrative aspects of games. We wish to argue that a better understanding of the nature of LND and the reasons it appears in games enables us to look at this phenomenon from a new perspective that was not, as of yet, considered in game studies literature or the popular discourse. The typical approach to LND presents it as a problem or a design flaw that needs to be avoided by the developers. In contrast to this, we suggest that LND can be seen as a source of inspiration for the creators as it inherently invites the developers and the players to reflect on the game structure. We start with a closer look at the notion of LND and present three ways it can be interpreted. In section two we analyze the reasons LND can appear in games (regardless of the developers’ intentions). Section three goes through some of the existing methods of dealing with LND. Here we argue that embracing LND as a result of some of the necessary tensions of game design can result in the creative victory of the developers. We finish the paper, in the fourth section, with a longer case study of Manhunt which we see as a good exemplification of the reinvigorating power of LND.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Walther, Bo Kampmann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-590060"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Grabarczyk, Pawel"],"keyword":["Gameplay","Ludo narrative dissonance","Ludology","Narrativity"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a game of twisted shouting ludo narrative dissonance revisited","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7557/23.6506","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-590060","identifier":[{"id":"85151974955","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3ad42715-20c8-45a5-a2a2-a9d080cddd5c"],"keyword":["Ludo-narrative dissonance","gameplay","games and violence","ludology","narrativity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-EE0A4DD8E6AE87C3BE60E46D2C5CB560"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7557/23.6506","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/225844316/Open_access_version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture, Media Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo Kampmann","key":"waltherpau","last":"Walther","locid":"62face49-4041-4f94-ac8e-7f2caa2e21f1","name":"Walther, Bo Kampmann","orcid":"0000-0003-0600-1779","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7557/23.6506","issn":["18666124"],"issue":"1","journal":"Eludamos","pages":"7-27","publisher":"Septentrio Academic Publishing","status":"p","title":"Eludamos","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3ad42715-20c8-45a5-a2a2-a9d080cddd5c"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A game of twisted shouting : ludo-narrative dissonance revisited","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-590060","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
