{"abstract":"Prior research on recruitment of women to computing has established that computing tasks involving People rather than Things have been perceived as much more appealing by female high-school students (potentially recruitable as university computing students). This paper changes the focus from prospective to current university students and presents the results of a new experiment that advances and moves beyond earlier research in two crucial respects. First of all, the participants of the experiment are N=152 university students, who already study computing, rather than general high-school students. Second of all, the choice between a People-themed versus an isomorphic Things-themed version of an educational task now pertains to real (in fact, mandatory) assignments that the students had to perform, rather than hypothetical tasks. The change of experimental context, design, and methodology allows us to complement previous findings related to recruitment with suggestions significant for computing educational activities. The overall findings of the new experiment are consistent with that of the previous one. We find that, also at university, there is a visible preference for choosing People themed over Things themed computing tasks amongst women. The results also expose considerable variation between tasks in the effect of gender observed. At the same time, male students, in general, seem to be either indifferent to the themes or to slightly prefer People versions. This suggests that educators should consider favoring People themed assignments over ones involving Things.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Marcher, Melissa Høegh","Christensen, Ingrid Maria","Grabarczyk, Pawel","Graversen, Therese","Brabrand, Claus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695242"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Computing education","Educational methodology","Gender preferences","Student engagement","Task selection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"computing educational activities involving people rather than things appeal more to women cs000000000001 appeal perspective","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.itu.dk/people/brabrand/ICER2021-retention.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-695242","identifier":[{"id":"85113674797","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4874b4cb-d20c-4dd6-ad55-ca99cfaed687"],"keyword":["- Computing education","- Educational methodology","- Gender preferences","- Student engagement","- Task selection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B68F3787E8224E3ACDE9C394B2126D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.itu.dk/people/brabrand/ICER2021-retention.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melissa Høegh","key":"marcherpau","last":"Marcher","locid":"2f4daeb6-5872-4c86-8f2d-5c5ffc3dd5fa","name":"Marcher, Melissa Høegh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid Maria","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Ingrid Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Therese","key":"graversenpau","last":"Graversen","locid":"1578b20c-b5d0-466f-b114-2582529ddc53","name":"Graversen, Therese","orcid":"0000-0002-2323-8965","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3446871.3469761","eisbn":["9781450383264"],"pages":"145-156","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 17th ACM Conference on International Computing Education Research (ICER 2021)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113674797"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4874b4cb-d20c-4dd6-ad55-ca99cfaed687"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Computing Educational Activities Involving People Rather Than Things Appeal More to Women (CS1 Appeal Perspective)","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695242","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we briefly present three perspectives from which the 4 phenomenon of context-sensitivity in language can be studied: structural, functional 5 and representational. Next, we describe the content of all papers included in the 6 volume and the relations of the papers to the three perspectives in question.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel","Ciecierski, Tadeusz"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383368"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Poland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Warsaw"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an introduction the architecture of context and context sensitivity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383368","ids":["itu-8eb4cd02-e5dc-4759-93a1-a0cfdd02c94d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0E22599B39735BEAE7872D54D097969E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"pl","key":"university of warsaw","loc":["Poland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Warsaw","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tadeusz","key":"ciecierskipau","last":"Ciecierski","name":"Ciecierski, Tadeusz","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783030344856"],"issn":["09244662"],"pages":"1-14","publisher":"Springer","series":"Studies in Linguistics and Philosophy","status":"p","subtitle":"Perspectives from Philosophy, Linguistics and Logic","title":"The Architecture of Context and Context-sensitivity"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85101977871"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8eb4cd02-e5dc-4759-93a1-a0cfdd02c94d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Introduction: The Architecture of Context and Context-Sensitivity","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383368","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The paper examines the phenomenon of retrogaming in the context of virtual reality. Author begins by introducing two categories of gaming nostalgia (homo- and hetero-medial) and argues that almost none of the existing VR experiences belong to the former category. In the next part of the paper, he applies two distinctions used by scholars to analyze nostalgia and discuss four case studies illustrating each of them. Author argues that in all of these cases the main focus of the developers concerns the external circumstances that the games of the past were played and not the games themselves (a factor that Mark P. Wolf called a “mode of exhibition”). He finishes the paper by discussing two problematic cases of retro VR experiences that do not fit the classification used previously. He argues that both of these cases simulate the mode of exhibition of contemporary retro practices.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Grabarczyk, Pawel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383283"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Nostalgia","Virtual reality","retrogaming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the past through stereoscopic lenses video games nostalgia in virtual reality","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4467/20843860PK.20.014.12378","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383283","ids":["itu-89c2954a-732c-48e0-ae05-da6d275403eb"],"keyword":["nostalgia","retrogaming","virtual reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C6C14361F33249E32250C4BD526E469B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/85541583/THE_PAST_THROUGH_STEREOSCOPIC_LENSES_VID.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4467/20843860PK.20.014.12378","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Games Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pawel","key":"grabarczykpau","last":"Grabarczyk","locid":"42147e05-f94c-471d-a889-c57a01e4bdd0","name":"Grabarczyk, Pawel","orcid":"0000-0002-1268-7474","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4467/20843860pk.20.014.12378","issn":["1895975X"],"issue":"44","journal":"Przegląd Kulturoznawczy","publisher":"Jagiellonian University Press","status":"p","title":"Przegląd Kulturoznawczy","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-89c2954a-732c-48e0-ae05-da6d275403eb"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The past through stereoscopic lenses. Video games nostalgia in virtual reality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383283","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
